  "body": "There are homes — and then there are opportunities that let you live fully while planning strategically for the future. This 728m² (more or less) north-facing coastal site is one of the rarest you’ll find: a beautiful, family-friendly residence with Resource Consent for subdivision already issued, offering both lifestyle and long-term value.\r\n\r\nStep inside and you’re greeted by spaces that feel effortlessly liveable, yet generous enough to grow with your family. Four bedrooms, three bathrooms, and three living areas flow naturally between sun-filled interiors and two expansive kwila decks. Imagine summer evenings hosting friends on the deck, children playing in the backyard, the smell of barbecue drifting across resort-style gardens illuminated with soft night lighting — this is the quintessential Kiwi indoor-outdoor lifestyle.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen and dining area form the heart of the home, with a new oven, dishwasher, timber flooring, and gas fireplace, seamlessly connecting to the second deck. The elevated master suite, complete with a modern ensuite, offers cityscape views — a quiet retreat above the bustle of daily life.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, a bedroom, bathroom, and living area create a flexible space that could serve as a self-contained apartment for extended family, teenagers, or future rental income. With ample parking, including space for a boat, and an electric retractable gate, convenience meets versatility.\r\n\r\nBeyond the home itself, the property’s subdivision potential sets it apart. With Resource Consent in motion, the land presents a clear path for future development — a rare combination of lifestyle today and strategic investment tomorrow.\r\n\r\nLocated on a quiet, dual-access street between the Bayswater and Devonport ferries, you’re just moments from Narrow Neck Beach, golf courses, parks, and top schools including Takapuna Grammar, Belmont Intermediate, Belmont Primary, and Vauxhall School.\r\n\r\nThis is more than a home; it’s a place to live, grow, and plan. A property that balances the everyday joys of Kiwi living with a strategic opportunity for the future — a combination that rarely comes to market.\r\n\r\nMove in now, enjoy the lifestyle, and embrace the potential.",
